From: ARMDeck <noreply@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: sm8250-oneplus-instantnoodle: limit the USB-C sink to 5 V

The connector node advertises PDO_VAR(5000, 12000, 5000) next to the 5 V
fixed PDO, so tcpm asks a USB PD charger for 9 V. On Android the OnePlus 8
never used PD above 5 V (its fast charging is Warp, 5 V / 6 A), and this
kernel has no charger driver that would adapt the PMIC's input settings to
a higher voltage. Keep only the 5 V / 3 A fixed PDO.

Tested on a OnePlus 8 (IN2013) on 2026-10-02 with the same change applied
to the DTB through fdtput: a Samsung 45 W charger (5 / 9 / 15 / 20 V and
PPS) negotiated USB PD at 5 V / 3 A, and the battery took about 0.9 A with
the Steam UI running.
---
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8250-oneplus-instantnoodle.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8250-oneplus-instantnoodle.dts
@@ -1294,11 +1294,15 @@
 					 PDO_FIXED_USB_COMM |
 					 PDO_FIXED_DATA_SWAP)>;
 
+		/*
+		 * 5 V only: the OnePlus 8 never took more than 5 V over USB PD on
+		 * Android (its fast charging is Warp, 5 V / 6 A), and without a
+		 * charger driver nothing else adapts the PMIC to a higher input.
+		 */
 		sink-pdos = <PDO_FIXED(5000, 3000,
 				       PDO_FIXED_DUAL_ROLE |
 				       PDO_FIXED_USB_COMM |
-				       PDO_FIXED_DATA_SWAP)
-				       PDO_VAR(5000, 12000, 5000)>;
+				       PDO_FIXED_DATA_SWAP)>;
 
 		ports {
 			#address-cells = <1>;
